{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49058", "qid": "gen-paper-05fc2361", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "7b9f084cc5fb", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2401.05299 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2401.05299 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- $\\chi^{2}$ compatibility test between unfolded distributions and predictions\n- Asimov dataset closure and bias stress tests of the unfolding procedure\n- Beeston-Barlow \"lite\" technique for limited MC sample-size statistical uncertainties\n- Maximum-likelihood (profile likelihood) fit with Poisson/Gaussian terms and Beeston-Barlow-lite MC-stat nuisances\n- Profile likelihood unfolding (PLU) for particle-level differential cross-sections\n- Statistical bootstrap optimization of regularization strength $\\tau$ via global correlation coefficient\n- Tikhonov (second-derivative) regularization of unfolding\n\nThese methods are used to ensure robustness and accuracy in the statistical analysis of the data.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2106.01676", "2111.08340", "2312.04450", "2401.05299"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2401.05299"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "seconds": 0.032}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:asimov-closure-test", "hepkg:method:beeston-barlow-lite", "hepkg:method:chi2-compatibility-test", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-unfolding", "hepkg:method:tau-bootstrap-optimization", "hepkg:method:tikhonov-regularisation"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:100411d82a177d30f46f14d8", "hepkg:evidence:26be0dcb2530342eb9d3ab92", "hepkg:evidence:7844f18131a2163b92f29c31", "hepkg:evidence:bc43d77dc3096b1f6fdb5029", "hepkg:evidence:e367c9a2ffd7cd4e6a4383de", "hepkg:evidence:ff656cd740682d4b7fb4db4b"]