{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49058", "qid": "gen-paper-aad389be", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "7b9f084cc5fb", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which systematic uncertainties does analysis 2604.27044 report?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2604.27044 reports the following systematic uncertainties:\n\n- Background prediction extrapolation bias uncertainty (CR mass sideband to SR)\n- Background prediction shape uncertainty parameterized via Fourier basis functions\n- Background prediction statistical variance uncertainty from finite CR/SR data and k-fold model spread\n- GloParT X->bb tagging efficiency scale factor uncertainty (10-25%)\n- H->bb branching fraction theoretical uncertainty (2.5%)\n- HH signal acceptance theoretical uncertainty (NNPDF parameters, muR/muF scale factor 2/0.5, parton shower ISR/FSR)\n- Jet energy scale (JES) and jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- Jet mass scale (JMS) and resolution (JMR) uncertainty for H->bb candidate AK8 jets\n- PDF set choice uncertainty on inclusive ggHH cross section (±1.5%)\n- Post-regression AK4 jet pT scale (1-2%) and resolution (4-8%) uncertainty\n- QCD muR/muF scale variation uncertainty on ggHH cross section (+2.1%,-4.9%)\n- QCD multijet background normalization uncertainty from unconstrained transfer factor profiling (merged, alphabet method)\n- Top quark mass value/definition (scheme) uncertainty on ggHH cross section (+4%,-18%)\n- Trigger efficiency scale factor, integrated luminosity, and pileup modeling uncertainty\n- alpha_S uncertainty on ggHH cross section (±1.7%)\n- b jet tagging efficiency and light-flavor misidentification rate uncertainty\n- qqHH inclusive cross section PDF and alpha_S uncertainty (±2.7%)\n- qqHH inclusive cross section QCD scale variation uncertainty (+0.05%,-0.03%)\n- ttbar background correction uncertainties (T_Xbb tagging score, tau32, recoil pT(jj)) in merged analysis\n\nThese uncertainties are documented in the analysis 2604.27044.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2106.01676", "2209.07327", "2308.02285", "2407.10549", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2604.27044"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 19, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:systematic:background-extrapolation-bias", "hepkg:systematic:background-shape-fourier", "hepkg:systematic:background-variance-kfold", "hepkg:systematic:bbtag-efficiency-sf", "hepkg:systematic:btag-efficiency", "hepkg:systematic:gghh-alphas", "hepkg:systematic:gghh-pdf", "hepkg:systematic:gghh-qcd-scale", "hepkg:systematic:gghh-topmass", "hepkg:systematic:hbb-brfrac", "hepkg:systematic:jes-jer", "hepkg:systematic:jetpt-regression-scale-resolution", "hepkg:systematic:jms-jmr", "hepkg:systematic:qcd-multijet-normalization-merged", "hepkg:systematic:qqhh-pdf-alphas", "hepkg:systematic:qqhh-qcdscale", "hepkg:systematic:signal-acceptance-theory", "hepkg:systematic:trigger-lumi-pileup", "hepkg:systematic:ttbar-correction-merged"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1d47cbb62109d0c66317c0d6", "hepkg:evidence:23c8532339d8e2e1ebd57a7b", "hepkg:evidence:36f7fdae160472d9764cbd5f", "hepkg:evidence:3704bc9cedde6ce7b57bbe05", "hepkg:evidence:37061f7a08aee642010f5e24", "hepkg:evidence:3c2ae45ce594da595d6e761e", "hepkg:evidence:59e0d5481bd66c42bdee1814", "hepkg:evidence:6add3537d12652f3fb36d10c", "hepkg:evidence:8aa8ba2ac07cf0cb33602f70", "hepkg:evidence:9cc96e64cc1a6c546c56828f", "hepkg:evidence:a39f08a8fd357caee527c0ff", "hepkg:evidence:c9d72f09bc3bc9f71cffadd1", "hepkg:evidence:d0ddae70a74efd378f825c81", "hepkg:evidence:e9f5d0945685c00fbacb7246", "hepkg:evidence:f665b938b57e77f88c208ea3", "hepkg:evidence:f7f895201ac6cfba32c2a548"], "seen_values": ["-18", "-25", "0.03", "0.05", "0.5", "1", "1.5", "1.7", "10", "2", "2.1", "2.5", "2.7", "2604.27044", "4", "4.9", "8", "acceptance", "ak4", "ak8", "alpha_s