{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49058", "qid": "gen-paper-cd49e95d", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "7b9f084cc5fb", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2208.12095 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2208.12095 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- $\\chi^{2}$ minimisation for Wilson-coefficient limits\n- Asimov dataset pseudo-experiments (500 smeared response matrices)\n- Bootstrap method for MC statistical uncertainty estimation\n- Extended Markov-chain Monte Carlo likelihood sampling\n- Fully Bayesian Unfolding (FBU)\n\nThese methods are documented in the paper as follows:\n\n- $\\chi^{2}$ minimisation for Wilson-coefficient limits: \"The limits on the Wilson coefficients are derived using a $\\chi^2$ minimisation.\"\n- Asimov dataset pseudo-experiments (500 smeared response matrices): \"The expected limits are evaluated using Asimov dataset pseudo-experiments, with 500 smeared response matrices.\"\n- Bootstrap method for MC statistical uncertainty estimation: \"The statistical uncertainties from the Monte Carlo simulation are estimated using the bootstrap method.\"\n- Extended Markov-chain Monte Carlo likelihood sampling: \"The likelihood is sampled using an extended Markov-chain Monte Carlo method.\"\n- Fully Bayesian Unfolding (FBU): \"The unfolded distributions are obtained using the Fully Bayesian Unfolding (FBU) method.\"", "answered": true, "papers": ["2208.12095"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2208.12095"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.032}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:asimov_pseudoexperiments", "hepkg:method:bootstrap_mc_stat", "hepkg:method:chi2_minimisation", "hepkg:method:fully_bayesian_unfolding", "hepkg:method:mcmc_sampling"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:2230b374e3fe95672fe68509", "hepkg:evidence:5210580b71fc107ad4d49832", "hepkg:evidence:82e9f886918fc8963ac3ebcd", "hepkg:evidence:95fe45d96477f9c98a148539"], "seen_values": ["2", "2208.12095", "5", "500", "asimov", "bayesian", "bootstrap", "carlo", "chi", "dataset", "estimation", "extended", "fbu", "for", "fully", "hepkg:method:asimov_pseudoexperiments", "hepkg:method:bootstrap_mc_stat", "hepkg:method:chi2_minimisation", "hepkg:method:fully_bayesian_unfolding", "hepkg:method:mcmc_sampling", "likelihood", "limits", "markov-chain", "matrices", "method", "minimisation", "monte", "pseudo-experiments", "response", "result_uses_statistical_method", "sampling", "smeared", "statistical", "statistical_method", "uncertainty", "unfolding", "wilson-coefficient"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 9443, "completion_tokens": 816, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 31.2952661216259, "reviews": [], "recovered_calls": 0, "cited": "", "abstention_challenged": false, "citation_corrected": false, "citation_disagrees": [], "invented_ids": [], "nudged": false, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 31.2952661216259, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 10259.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "retrieved_label_recall": 1.0, "retrieved_entities": 5.0, "mentioned_label_recall": 1.0, "truncation_loss_labels": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 5.0, "evidence_quotes": 4.0}}
{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49058", "qid": "gen-paper-cf39c15d", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "7b9f084cc5fb", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which observables does analysis 2605.14245 measure?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2605.14245 measures the following observables:\n\n- \\( f_{CP}^{Htt} \\) (Htt CP-odd effective fractional cross section)\n- \\( f_{\\Lambda1} \\) (HVV effective fractional cross section)\n- \\( f_{\\Lambda1}^{Z\\gamma} \\) (HVV effective fractional cross section)\n- \\( f_{a2} \\) (HVV effective fractional cross section)\n- \\( f_{a3} \\) (CP-odd HVV effective fractional cross section)\n- \\( f_{a3}^{ggH} \\) (effective CP-odd Hgg cross section fraction)\n- \\( \\mu_V \\) (signal strength modifier for VBF+VH production)\n- \\( \\mu_f \\) (signal strength modifier for ggH+ttH production)\n\nThese observables are related to the effective fractional cross sections and signal strength modifiers in the context of Higgs boson production and decay.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2205.05120", "2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2605.14245"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 8, "error": null, "seconds": 0.036}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:parameter:f_a2", "hepkg:parameter:f_a3", "hepkg:parameter:f_a3_gg_h", "hepkg:parameter:f_cp_htt", "hepkg:parameter:f_lambda1", "hepkg:parameter:f_lambda1_zgamma", "hepkg:parameter:mu_f", "hepkg:parameter:mu_v"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1c0e1f9141daacbe6a8690e7", "hepkg:evidence:47663ced922c5f00d7720e3f", "hepkg:evidence:6e96b57a70e1e4170b12143d", "hepkg:evidence:77f8b5891174fa17244e3f7a", "hepkg:evidence:8a1ec09caa80ebfb1b565574", "hepkg:evidence:e346e781070b21312e9cbaa9"], "seen_values": ["2605.14245", "cp-odd", "cross", "effective", "f_a2", "f_a3", "f_cp", "f_lambda1", "fraction", "fractional", "ggh", "hepkg:pa