{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49058", "qid": "gen-paper-e588a3a8", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "7b9f084cc5fb", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2602.18611 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2602.18611 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Asimov data set method for expected results\n- Asymptotic approximation for 68%/95% CL intervals (q<1, q<3.84; q<2.30, q<5.99 for 2D)\n- Barlow-Beeston lite approach for MC statistical uncertainties in simulated templates\n- CMS Combine statistical analysis tool (RooFit/RooStats)\n- Correlation matrix extraction from second derivatives of q(alpha) around best fit\n- Maximum likelihood fits to extract SMEFT Wilson coefficient constraints\n- Moment matching procedure to determine simplified-likelihood parameters (dimidated Gaussian)\n- Principal component analysis (PCA) of Hessian matrix to derive constrained SMEFT eigenvector directions\n- Profile likelihood ratio test statistic q(alpha)\n- SM compatibility p-value from chi-square distribution of q(alpha_SM)\n- Simplified likelihood procedure (Gaussian/dimidated-Gaussian approximation) for SMEFT constraints", "answered": true, "papers": ["2602.18611"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2602.18611"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 11, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:barlow_beeston_lite", "hepkg:statistical_method:asimov_dataset_method", "hepkg:statistical_method:asymptotic_approximation_cl_intervals", "hepkg:statistical_method:combine_roofit_roostats_tool", "hepkg:statistical_method:hessian_correlation_extraction", "hepkg:statistical_method:maximum_likelihood_fit_smeft", "hepkg:statistical_method:moment_matching_procedure", "hepkg:statistical_method:pca_hessian_smeft", "hepkg:statistical_method:profile_likelihood_ra